  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This issue can be frequently seen when turning around in VR both via controller and physically and then starting to walk forwards. \nOn further inspection it seems like that any deviation from looking straight foward will result in an upper body rotation that makes you walk slightly sideways. Even worse sometimes this can stack multiple times and break your upper body rotation completely. \nThis seems to be an issue with the IK not resetting your body rotation back to its initial rotation when starting to walk.\nYou can easily force this to break by turning around and walking forward for a moment over and over until (keep pressing forward for a short moment over and over) you'll see your avatar rotation break in varies strengths up to the point that your entire body turns sideways. This very frequently happens when playing Among Us due to coming into a room, doing a quick thing and immediately turning while at the same time walking forward away from said room again. I frequently have to stop for a moment (so you go back into the normal IK-less resting pose before IK starts kicking in) to force my body rotation to reset and then continue walking. It's incredibly annoying.\n\nhttps://gfycat.com/splendidsoupyhapuku",
